  "prefLabel": "Rev 601.24 Full statistical revaluation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 601.24 \"Full statistical revaluation\" means the process of a revaluation of all taxable and nontaxable properties in a municipality, using existing property data, to arrive at full and true value as of April 1. The term includes “statistical update” and “statistical reassessment.”\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Rev 600) #10581, eff 5-1-14; ss by #13916, eff 3-28-24 (formerly Rev 601.25) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Rev 600)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev600.html"
